---
args: { scope: DisputeScope, rules: ApplicableDisputeRules, evidence: QuestionEvidenceLedger, pages: EvidencePage[] }
returns: ConditionalDisposition
---
Apply the transaction-time rule only to established facts. For every unresolved dispositive premise, show the outcome under each plausible value and identify what evidence could distinguish them. Missing evidence from an incomplete partition is not adverse proof. Require current ledger reconciliation before an added remedy for any payment reversal; require configured outage interval and deadline overlap before extending a deadline. Route interpretations beyond documented delegation to an authorized reviewer.
